                <pb facs="0769" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg709"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the embassy note of the 19th
                    ultimo to Mr. Adee, and to previous correspondence on the subject of the tax
                    levied on United States vessels entering and clearing from Canadian ports, I
                    have the honor to inform you that the question is still under consideration and
                    will receive prompt attention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
